# Queue at submit (Cursor / Opus / Grok)

Policy SoT for queue/land ops: `~/.agents/skills/sume-gt-mq/SKILL.md`.
The file keeps its old name; Graphite (`gt`, the `merge-queue` label) is
retired for `sume` since 2026-10-30.

## Locked (2026-10-30)

After **`gh stack submit --auto --open`**, from the author clone at the
stack tip:

```bash
cstack-gt-wait-merge --rm <job-slug>
```

It links the PR chain into one GitHub stack, waits for `validate` on every
layer, then queues the whole stack (`gh stack merge`; one PR:
`gh pr merge --auto --squash`).

| Prefer | Avoid |
|--------|--------|
| **`cstack-gt-wait-merge`** | Hand-rolled `sleep` + `grep` / `gh pr checks` loops |
| Run it from the **tip** | Queueing only the base PR |
| Author **stays** until every layer is on `main` | STOP after queueing |

**A queue removal is land, not a reason to stop.** Each layer has its own
queue run. A red layer leaves the queue with every layer above it; layers
below it still land. Fix, `gh stack sync`, run the helper again.

